## Endpoint Reference (use these EXACT paths)

| Action | Method | Path | Rate Limit |
|---|---|---|---|
| Validate auth | GET | `/store` | normal |
| List catalog products | GET | `/products?category_id={ids}` | 30/60s unauth |
| Catalog product detail | GET | `/products/{id}` | 30/60s unauth |
| Catalog variant | GET | `/products/variant/{id}` | 30/60s unauth |
| Size guide | GET | `/products/{id}/sizes?unit=cm` | 30/60s unauth |
| Categories | GET | `/categories` | 30/60s unauth |
| List my products | GET | `/store/products` | 120/min |
| Create Sync Product | POST | `/store/products` | 120/min |
| Modify Sync Product | PUT | `/store/products/{id}` | **10/60s** |
| Delete Sync Product | DELETE | `/store/products/{id}` | 120/min |
| Create order | POST | `/orders` | 120/min |
| Get order | GET | `/orders/{id}` | 120/min |
| Confirm order | POST | `/orders/{id}/confirm` | 120/min |
| Cancel order | DELETE | `/orders/{id}` | 120/min |
| Estimate order costs | POST | `/orders/estimate-costs` | 120/min |
| Shipping rates | POST | `/shipping/rates` | 120/min |
| Tax rates | POST | `/tax/rates` | 120/min |
| Get webhooks | GET | `/webhooks` | 120/min |
| Set webhooks | POST | `/webhooks` | 120/min |
| Disable webhooks | DELETE | `/webhooks` | 120/min |

**Reference by external ID:** prefix with `@`. Example: `GET /orders/@internal-order-uuid-1234`.

---

## Order Lifecycle (memorize this state machine)

```
Customer checkout
      │
      ▼
[Quote shipping]   ── POST /shipping/rates
      │
      ▼
[Estimate costs]   ── POST /orders/estimate-costs
      │
      ▼
[Show total to customer in MXN]
      │
      ▼
[Customer confirms]
      │
      ▼
[Create as DRAFT]  ── POST /orders   (DO NOT confirm yet)
      │
      ▼
[Validate locally] (stock, address, totals)
      │
      ▼
[Charge customer] (Stripe/Conekta/etc.)
      │
      ▼
[Confirm order]   ── POST /orders/{id}/confirm
      │
      ▼
[Wait for webhooks]
      │
      ├─→ order_updated   → update local status
      ├─→ package_shipped → notify customer + tracking
      ├─→ order_failed    → refund + alert ops
      └─→ order_canceled  → refund
```

**Cancelable states:** `draft`, `pending`, `onhold`. Once `inprocess` → cannot cancel.

---

## Sync Product Rules

- Max **100 sync variants** per sync product. Split into multiple if needed.
- Every variant needs: `variant_id` (from catalog), `retail_price` (string), `files[]`, `external_id`.
- Print files: pass `url` (Printful downloads it) or `id` (already in File Library).
- Filenames in files must end with `.png`, `.jpg`, or `.pdf`. Use 300 DPI minimum.
- For inside labels: use `template_type: "native"`. Custom labels are deprecated (April 2020).
- **NEVER** try to sync jewelry. Not supported via API.
- `PUT /store/products/{id}` capped at **10 req/60s**. Batch changes locally before pushing.

```typescript
// Schema for creating a sync product
import { z } from 'zod';

export const SyncProductInput = z.object({
  external_id: z.string().min(1),
  name: z.string().min(1).max(255),
  thumbnail: z.string().url(),
  variants: z.array(z.object({
    external_id: z.string(),
    variant_id: z.number().int().positive(),    // FROM CATALOG, not product_id
    retail_price: z.string().regex(/^\d+\.\d{2}$/),
    sku: z.string().optional(),
    files: z.array(z.object({
      type: z.enum(['default', 'back', 'sleeve_left', 'sleeve_right', 'label_inside']),
      url: z.string().url(),
    })).min(1),
  })).max(100),
});
```

